WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:04.300
This example uses a cross join with a filter only to
demonstrate that joins can

00:00:04.326 --> 00:00:10.028
multiply rows In real Spark work joins can be
expensive because

00:00:10.054 --> 00:00:15.557
Spark may need to move data so matching keys are
together Before joining

00:00:15.583 --> 00:00:20.465
large datasets ask whether the join keys are correct
whether the grain is controlled and

00:00:20.491 --> 00:00:22.833
whether one side is small enough to broadcast
